  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.54,
      "end_seconds": 4.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Hello, sorry about the delay, do sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.07,
      "end_seconds": 10.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Hi there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.83,
      "end_seconds": 13.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.14,
      "end_seconds": 21.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "It's burning when I pass urine. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.55,
      "end_seconds": 27.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.74,
      "end_seconds": 34.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Ah, probably ten days. Yeah. I've been putting this off for weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.61,
      "end_seconds": 37.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Ah. Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.48,
      "end_seconds": 53.99,
      "duration_seconds": 14.51,
      "text": "I'd say every other day. I've been going to the toilet often too. Oh, and a dull ache low in my tummy. That's been about the same, five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.12,
      "end_seconds": 65.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.88,
      "end_seconds": 80.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.28,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.18,
      "end_seconds": 84.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.61,
      "end_seconds": 90.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.59,
      "end_seconds": 95.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.49,
      "end_seconds": 103.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.35,
      "text": "I'm on fluoxetine, 20 milligrams, every morning for my mood. Cranberry juice, daily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.6,
      "end_seconds": 107.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.04,
      "end_seconds": 111.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "I've had depression, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.06,
      "end_seconds": 118.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Ah. Okay, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.66,
      "end_seconds": 124.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "No, um, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.03,
      "end_seconds": 126.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Any sign of fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.62,
      "end_seconds": 132.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Erm, not that I've noticed, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.94,
      "end_seconds": 139.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "And what about back pain, blood in the urine or vaginal discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.75,
      "end_seconds": 147.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Oh, no, no back pain, blood in the urine or vaginal discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.6,
      "end_seconds": 154.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.96,
      "end_seconds": 161.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "No, you know, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.83,
      "end_seconds": 174.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.86,
      "end_seconds": 184.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.77,
      "end_seconds": 215.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.82,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 123 over 68, height 162 centimetres, respiratory rate 15. And weight 73 kilos, BMI works out to 27.8, pulse 83."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.96,
      "end_seconds": 221.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.0,
      "end_seconds": 224.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Alright, nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.99,
      "end_seconds": 246.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with slight tenderness just above the pubic bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.36,
      "end_seconds": 261.31,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Okay, so my impression is this: I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at an uncomplicated urinary infection or vaginal irritation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.41,
      "end_seconds": 265.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.72,
      "end_seconds": 274.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an uncomplicated urinary infection, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.14,
      "end_seconds": 314.48,
      "duration_seconds": 21.34,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a urine dipstick for burning urine. You'll be taking nitrofurantoin, 100 milligrams, twice a day, three days. That should help with urinary infection. Drink plenty of water and avoid holding urine. Let's review you if it is not better in three days. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.56,
      "end_seconds": 319.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Okay, so good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}